      ],
      "chunk_id": "47b76ced-caf6-4234-b966-1a9cbde9e540",
      "content": "Approval Requirements\n\nEmployees must receive manager approval before changing their regular work location. A temporary change within the same country for fewer than 15 business days may be approved by the manager. Longer changes require People Operations review.\n\nManagers should consider team coverage, customer needs, time zone overlap, and data handling requirements before approving remote work.",
      "department_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002001",
      "document_id": "HR-003",
      "project_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000019",
      "tenant_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002801"
    },
    {
      "access_roles": [
        "Employee",
        "Sales Representative",
        "Manager",
        "HR Admin",
        "IT/Admin"
      ],
      "chunk_id": "483a6ce6-f231-4b14-9190-948b5d6cd35b",
      "content": "Vacation Approval Workflow\n\nVacation requests of 1 to 5 business days should be submitted at least 10 business days in advance. Requests longer than 5 business days should be submitted at least 20 business days in advance.\n\nManagers approve vacation based on business coverage, project deadlines, and fairness across the team. Managers should not deny vacation without explaining the business reason.",
      "department_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002001",
      "document_id": "HR-002",
      "project_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000019",
      "tenant_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002801"
    },
    {
      "access_roles": [
        "Employee",
        "Sales Representative",
        "Manager",
        "HR Admin",
        "IT/Admin"
      ],
      "chunk_id": "4d9b5b5a-6038-4f40-9321-f262d3aa7fd9",
      "content": "Cross-Border Work\n\nNorthstar does not guarantee approval for work from any country. Temporary cross-border work requires People Operations review before travel. The company does not maintain a formal visa or immigration policy in the employee knowledge base.\n\nRequests to work outside Canada or the United States are considered ambiguous until People Operations reviews tax, employment, and security implications.",
      "department_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002001",
      "document_id": "HR-003",
      "project_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000019",
      "tenant_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002801"
    },
    {
      "access_roles": [
        "Employee",
        "Manager",
        "HR Admin",
        "IT/Admin"
      ],
      "chunk_id": "6b97676d-c44e-480a-8d38-54df3d81974c",
      "content": "Travel Booking\n\nEmployees should book business travel at least 14 days before departure when practical. Airfare, hotel, and ground transportation should be booked through the approved travel tool unless an emergency, accessibility need, or customer requirement makes that impractical.\n\nManagers approve travel before booking when the trip is not already listed in the department plan. Travel booked after manager denial is not reimbursable unless the denial is reversed in writing.",
      "department_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002011",
      "document_id": "OPS-001",
      "project_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000019",
      "tenant_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002801"
    },
    {
      "access_roles": [
        "Employee",
        "Sales Representative",
        "Manager",
        "HR Admin",
        "IT/Admin"
      ],
      "chunk_id": "4ec63d09-594a-4640-b1f7-5db5f5b9b238",
      "content": "Work Model\n\nNorthstar supports hybrid work and approved remote work. Employees assigned to Toronto, Montreal, or New York offices are expected to attend office collaboration days when scheduled by their department.\n\nRemote employees may work from approved locations in Canada or the United States if their role, tax location, and security requirements support remote work.",
      "department_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002001",
      "document_id": "HR-003",
      "project_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000019",
      "tenant_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002801"
    }
  ],
